{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b1b1074e-5e52-4c2a-9f31-2f0a5d3c7a10",
    "name": "Bibliotheque - Module Reservation (seance 2)",
    "description": "Collection complete et automatisee du module Reservation.\n\n=== ORDRE D'EXECUTION ===\n  1 Authentification   : identifiants deja remplis, les jetons se rangent seuls\n  2 Le jeu de donnees  : afficher L1-L5, A1-A3 et les emprunts\n  3 Parcours nominal   : creer, consulter, lister, filtrer, annuler\n  4 Regles de gestion  : RG-01 a RG-06, chacune declenchee volontairement\n  5 Validation et 404  : champs manquants, ressources absentes\n  6 Securite           : 401 sans jeton, 403 sans le role\n  7 Nettoyage          : remise a zero\n\nS'execute d'un bloc avec le Collection Runner, de haut en bas.\nRien a saisir : identifiants, identifiants de livres et d'adherents sont deja\ndans les variables de collection.\n\n=== PREREQUIS ===\nLe backend de la branche feature/reservation-tasse-ulruch doit tourner sur le\nport 8080. L'image Docker de la seance 1 ne contient pas /api/reservations :\nelle repondrait 401 a toute la collection. La requete 1.4 le detecte et le dit.\n\n=== DONNEES ATTENDUES EN BASE (fixtures-reservation.sql) ===\n  L1 (201) : livre DISPONIBLE, 3 exemplaires, aucun emprunt en cours\n  L2 (202), L3 (203), L4 (204), L5 (205) : empruntes par A3 et non rendus\n  A1 (301) a1_reservataire : reservataire principal\n  A2 (302) a2_quota       : celui qui saturera son quota\n  A3 (303) a3_emprunteur  : l'emprunteur, il detient L2 a L5\n  Mot de passe des trois adherents : admin123",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8080" },
    { "key": "L1", "value": "201" },
    { "key": "L2", "value": "202" },
    { "key": "L3", "value": "203" },
    { "key": "L4", "value": "204" },
    { "key": "L5", "value": "205" },
    { "key": "A1", "value": "301" },
    { "key": "A2", "value": "302" },
    { "key": "A3", "value": "303" },
    { "key": "token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "tokenA1", "value": "" },
    { "key": "reservationA1", "value": "" },
    { "key": "reservationA2", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1 - Authentification",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1.1 POST /authenticate - admin",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', json.jwtToken);",
                  "pm.test('Un jeton JWT est renvoye et range dans {{token}}', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(json.jwtToken).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Le compte porte le role Admin', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(JSON.stringify(json.user.role)).to.include('Admin');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"admin\",\n  \"password\": \"admin123\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/authenticate", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["authenticate"] },
            "description": "Premiere requete de la collection. Les identifiants sont deja saisis. Le jeton part dans {{token}} : toutes les routes /admin/** l'utilisent ensuite sans intervention."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1.2 POST /authenticate - A1, simple adherent",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('tokenA1', json.jwtToken);",
                  "pm.test('Le compte porte le role User, pas Admin', function () {",
                  "    const roles = JSON.stringify(json.user.role);",
                  "    pm.expect(roles).to.include('User');",
                  "    pm.expect(roles).to.not.include('Admin');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"a1_reservataire\",\n  \"password\": \"admin123\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/authenticate", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["authenticate"] },
            "description": "Range le jeton dans {{tokenA1}}. Le dossier 6 s'en sert pour montrer la difference entre etre authentifie et avoir le role."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1.3 POST /authenticate - mot de passe errone -> 401",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401 Unauthorized', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(401); });",
                  "pm.test('Aucun jeton n est renvoye', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.not.include('jwtToken');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"admin\",\n  \"password\": \"mauvais_mot_de_passe\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/authenticate", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["authenticate"] },
            "description": "Le mot de passe est compare par BCrypt : un mot de passe errone ne passe pas."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1.4 Remise a zero des reservations de A1 et A2",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Diagnostic avant tout : un 401 ou un 404 ici signifie que le backend",
                  "// lance n'est pas celui de la seance 2. L'image Docker de la seance 1",
                  "// ne contient pas /api/reservations et rejette tout le reste.",
                  "pm.test('Le module Reservation est bien deploye (sinon : mauvais backend)', function () {",
                  "    if (pm.response.code === 401 || pm.response.code === 404) {",
                  "        throw new Error('Le backend qui repond sur ' + pm.collectionVariables.get('baseUrl') +",
                  "            ' ne contient pas /api/reservations (code ' + pm.response.code + '). ' +",
                  "            'Lancez le jar de la branche feature/reservation-tasse-ulruch, ' +",
                  "            'pas le conteneur bibliotheque-backend de la seance 1.');",
                  "    }",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Rend la collection rejouable. Sans cette purge, la deuxieme execution",
                  "// echouerait des RG-02 : A1 aurait deja une reservation active sur L2,",
                  "// heritee du tour precedent.",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    const base = pm.collectionVariables.get('baseUrl');",
                  "    [pm.collectionVariables.get('A1'), pm.collectionVariables.get('A2')].forEach(function (id) {",
                  "        pm.sendRequest(base + '/api/reservations?adherentId=' + id, function (err, res) {",
                  "            if (err || !res) { return; }",
                  "            res.json().forEach(function (r) {",
                  "                pm.sendRequest({ url: base + '/api/reservations/' + r.id, method: 'DELETE' }, function () {});",
                  "            });",
                  "        });",
                  "    });",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/reservations", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "reservations"] },
            "description": "Deux roles : verifier que le bon backend repond, et purger les reservations de A1 et A2 pour que la collection reparte toujours du meme etat."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2 - Afficher le jeu de donnees",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "2.1 GET /admin/books - les cinq livres",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "const livres = pm.response.json();",
                  "const trouver = function (id) { return livres.find(function (l) { return l.bookId === id; }); };",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('L1 est DISPONIBLE', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(trouver(201).noOfCopies).to.be.above(0);",
                  "});",
                  "[202, 203, 204, 205].forEach(function (id) {",
                  "    pm.test('Le livre ' + id + ' est indisponible', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect(trouver(id).noOfCopies).to.eql(0);",
                  "    });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/books", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["admin", "books"] },
            "description": "noOfCopies est la seule chose que regarde RG-01 : > 0 vaut disponible, 0 vaut reservable. Le jeton vient de 1.1."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2.2 GET /admin/books/{{L1}} - le livre disponible",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "pm.test('C est bien L1', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().bookName).to.include('L1');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/books/{{L1}}", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["admin", "books", "{{L1}}"] },
            "description": "Route annotee @PreAuthorize(\"hasRole('Admin')\") : elle exige le jeton admin, pas celui d'un adherent."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2.3 GET /admin/users - les trois adherents",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "const users = pm.response.json();",
                  "[301, 302, 303].forEach(function (id) {",
                  "    pm.test('L adherent ' + id + ' existe', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect(users.some(function (u) { return u.userId === id; })).to.be.true;",
                  "    });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/users", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["admin", "users"] },
            "description": "A1, A2 et A3 doivent apparaitre, avec le role User."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2.4 GET /borrow - les emprunts en cours",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "const enCours = pm.response.json().filter(function (e) { return e.returnDate === null; });",
                  "pm.test('Au moins quatre emprunts non rendus', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(enCours.length).to.be.at.least(4);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/borrow", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["borrow"] },
            "description": "returnDate a null signifie « emprunte et non rendu ». C'est ce qui justifie que L2 a L5 soient a zero exemplaire."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2.5 GET /borrow/user/{{A3}} - A3 detient L2 a L5",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "const emprunts = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('A3 detient quatre livres', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(emprunts.length).to.eql(4);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Ce sont bien L2, L3, L4 et L5', function () {",
                  "    const ids = emprunts.map(function (e) { return e.bookId; }).sort();",
                  "    pm.expect(ids).to.eql([202, 203, 204, 205]);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Aucun n est rendu', function () {",
                  "    emprunts.forEach(function (e) { pm.expect(e.returnDate).to.be.null; });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/borrow/user/{{A3}}", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["borrow", "user", "{{A3}}"] },
            "description": "A3 est l'emprunteur du tableau : c'est lui qui rend L2 a L5 indisponibles, donc reservables."
          }
        },
        {
